<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Constance</h1><p class="st-meta">1192 CE – 1548 CE (approx.) · capital Konstanz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Lake Constance city that hosted the great Council of 1414 to 1418, which ended the Western Schism and burned Jan Hus, before Austria absorbed it in 1548.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstanz">Constance</a> was a Roman fort and from about 600 the seat of the largest diocese in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Its citizens gradually freed themselves from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>'s rule, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> emperors granted privileges, so that by the late 12th century it was treated as an imperial city.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Merchants and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guilds</a> shared power in the council. The city's fine linen was sold across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and it was a member of Swabian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a> city leagues. From 1414 to 1418 it hosted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-constance">Council of Constance</a>, which elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-martin-v">Pope Martin V</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-schism">Western Schism</a>, and burned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-hus">Jan Hus</a>. In the 1520s the city adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambrosius-blarer">Ambrosius Blarer</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meersburg">Meersburg</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>As a member of the defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-league">Schmalkaldic League</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstanz">Constance</a> was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> in 1548 and given to the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, losing its freedom and returning to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a>. It stayed in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/further-austria">Further Austria</a> until passing to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> in 1806.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="imperial city, 1192 CE – 1548 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">imperial city</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.42%;width:7.08%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1192 CE – 1548 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>imperial city</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Konstanz</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, Reformed Protestantism (1527 to 1548)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Alemannic German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Germany</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Konstanz</dd></dl></aside></div>

